From f3caae0990ec4c06ac904b627b03347137f275af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlyRien <9572419+CharlyRien@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:06:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] Lab: XCL_DISPATCHX_FLAGS=1 (off) launches a DispatchX
 with thread dimensions as whole groups

With flag 0x20 (USE_THREAD_DIMENSIONS) x, y, z are thread counts: the console launches
ceil(count / numthreads) groups and leaves the lanes past the count out of EXEC. XCL dropped the
flags and launched the counts as groups (32-64 times the groups the builder's passes want). With
the switch, DispatchX passes its flags on (a put-off dispatch keeps them) and the counts become
whole groups of the program's console numthreads (kept per pipeline from the console CS); a
pipeline whose group shape is not known is not launched. The lanes past the count in the last
group still run: masking them needs the translator (PR #3015) and is not here.

Host side of XCL PR #2610 (KDenKC, GPL-3.0-or-later: dispatch_groups, pso_threads, the deferred
flags), behind a switch; numthreads kept in a map of its own instead of widening PSO_USER_SGPRS.
Not in TRANSLATOR_SOURCES (recomp/pso.rs, bind.rs, list_x.rs, real.rs).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
